Dots (B2,B4,B8) gives flexibility to form Dot chows.\n3. Keeping T6 and T8 allows possible Bamboo chows with draws like T7,T9.\n\nThus, **Play T1**.\n\n**Reason:**  \nDiscarding T1 removes a terminal that doesn\u2019t fit well with my current hand structure and melds (which are mid-range Bamboos). Keeping Dots and mid Bamboos offers more chances to form chows and aim for Half Flush or Mixed Straight patterns. T1\u2019s low availability (only 2 left) also reduces its utility for me, whereas other tiles have better remaining counts.\n\n**Answer:** Play T1"}
